{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/intrusive-fantasy-a-case-study-of-shadowhunters.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"en":["Intrusive Fantasy: A Case Study of Shadowhunters"]},"homepage":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling","type":"Text","label":{"en":["Intrusive Fantasy: A Case Study of Shadowhunters"]},"format":"text/html"}],"metadata":[{"label":{"en":["Description"]},"value":{"en":["Annotations by Bridie Pickering"]}},{"label":{"en":["Language"]},"value":{"en":["English"]}}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10","type":"Canvas","duration":58,"annotations":[{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/manifests/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters-canvas10-1","type":"AnnotationPage","label":{"en":["Default"]},"items":[{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"The notion of protecting the Human World from the Demon World is what informs the audience of the secondary world that exists on top of the existing world.\nClary's discovery of the intrusive world is described as her learning the truth about the world, because her true \"Sight\" allows her to see the monsters that have been infiltrating the human world. \nThis kind of fantasy is known as intrusive fantasy - where a secondary world begins to intrude on the existing world, with the intent of infiltrating or destroying the existing world.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=0,7"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"In intrusive fantasy, the secondary and existing worlds are often involved in conflicts, with a group that belongs to both worlds acting as the sentries, preventing the secondary world from crushing the existing world. \nIn Shadowhunters, the Nephilim are the ones preventing the demons from crossing into the existing world. They are from the world of Angels and Demons, as they are part Angel, and they are also part human. Their humanity gives them a\nreason to protect the human world from the Demon threat. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=8,11"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Clary learning that she's part angel helps her to make sense of the strange things she's been seeing, but it also means she becomes one of the guardians of the human world. Instead of just being a normal person, she'd suddenly being hunted by Demons, and having to hunt them in return. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=12,22"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"For Clary and the other Nephilim, they have a mission to defend the human world. If they fail todispatch demons, the human world will become overrun with them.\nThe other Nephilim have been raised as warriors, but Clary was raised in the human world - her mother wanted to protect her from the demon world, and her father. For Clary, coming to terms with the mission she faces is incredibly difficult.","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=23,28"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Clary wants to stay far away from the battle between the Nephilim and the Demons, but her very existence involves her. She tries to keep her life separate from the Shadowhunters, but once she's seen the truth, she cannot ignore it any longer.\nThat, and her mother was kidnapped, so she requires help from the Nephilim in order to see her safely returned.\n","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=29,39"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"These clips make it clear that the Nephilim do not only face demonic threats, but also other Nephilim that are fighting against them, and trying to achieve their own goals. The Nephilim are at war with themselves too, not just the demons. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Rules","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=40,50"},{"@context":"http://www.w3.org/ns/anno.jsonld","type":"Annotation","motivation":["commenting","tagging"],"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10/page1","body":[{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Clary's acceptance of the mission is a key moment for her character. It shows that despite everything she's seen, she's willing to join the fight for the Nephilim, to save the human world. Even as she looks terrified, there's a steely determination in her eyes. She is, after all, a Nephilim, and they are born to be warriors. ","format":"text/plain","motivation":"commenting"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Television Show","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Worldbuilding","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Magic System","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"},{"type":"TextualBody","value":"Intrusive Fantasy","format":"text/plain","purpose":"tagging","motivation":"tagging"}],"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10#t=51,53"}]}],"items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters-canvas10/paintings","type":"AnnotationPage","items":[{"id":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters-canvas10/paintings","type":"Annotation","motivation":"painting","body":{"id":"https://youtu.be/mexud7kJ6Es?si=CoBiquYjnILzkx6a","type":"Video","format":"unknown","duration":58},"target":"https://Bridie219.github.io/Storytelling/intrusive_fantasy_a_case_study_of_shadowhunters/canvas/10"}]}]}]}